[Music]  knife making is almost meditative for me  there's a lot of passion behind it  there's a lot of hard work behind it and  it's not just something that you kind of  just brush off like oh this is just a  knife  [Music]  people hands touch this knife people  pour their passion and their soul inside  of these products  the art of blacksmithing has a very long  history  our notion of what it means to be  civilized is to have metallurgy to have  the ability to transform the natural  world  when somebody used my knife i wanted to  see damn  golly this is a bad ass knife  come here let me show you something  well let me tell you what quentin  middleton does i make knives for a  living  who knew  [Music]  i am from saint stephen south carolina  that's maybe about an hour away from  charleston south carolina we're in  basically my backyard  this is my studio this is where it all  goes down where every last one of my  knives is made  [Music]  why does quentin middleton make knives  because i love it it's just a voice love  from watching fantasy movies like star  wars he-man conan like it just piqued my  imagination  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  i've watched him go from making kung fu  weapons out of lawn mower blades  to chef's knives to being a a serious  businessman like a force to be reckoned  with  i love color i love pops of color i love  the reds the blues the greens that's my  personality and i like my knives to look  sexy  the knife we'll be making today will be  an 8 inch chef knife it will be damascus  damascus steel is a set of techniques  that involve the layering of iron upon  iron upon iron creating this more  complex and more durable structure  i will be using two types of steel it  basically is going to give you contrast  between shiny and dark you will see a  bunch of swirls in it that's what make  it pretty  first i'm measuring each one of these a  piece of steel each one of them is cut  at five inches  and then i'm chopping up in the chop saw  i 